    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Well, what brings me in is that I just feel like I'm constantly running on a motor lately. Like, I'll finish one thing at school—I'm a special education teacher, by the way, been doing it for years. I actually had this one kid, Tommy, just the sweetest boy but he would always try to eat the crayons, especially the blue ones, no idea why. Anyway, I finish one thing at school or at home, and I immediately jump into the next thing without ever being able to shut myself off. It's exhausting, but I just can't stop. I bought a new lawnmower last weekend, thinking maybe yard work would help burn it off, but I ended up mowing my neighbor's lawn too because I just couldn't sit down.",
