    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "During this time, how has your sleep been?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Sleep? Um, I haven't really noticed anything different, honestly. I just kind of keep going until I crash. My wife did just buy us one of those new mattresses, though. You know, the ones that come vacuum-sealed in a box? It is just wild how they fit a whole king-size bed into a cardboard box. The delivery guy—poor kid, he looked like he was maybe 19, tops—was just sweating bullets trying to get it up our front steps. I actually ran out and helped him carry it, and then I gave him a Gatorade from the garage fridge. Lemon-lime, obviously, because that's the only good flavor. My daughter drinks the blue ones, which always reminds me of Tommy and the blue crayons, but... wait, what did you ask me? Oh, right, sleep. Yeah, I don't know, I guess I haven't really paid attention to it. It seems fine?",
