    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you frequently misplace or have trouble keeping track of items you need every day, like your keys, wallet, or phone?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Keys and wallet? No, I don't think so. I actually have this little leather tray right by the front door where I put everything the second I walk in. My daughter bought it for me for Father's Day a few years ago. She got it custom stamped with my initials, but the guy at the craft fair accidentally stamped 'J.R.' instead of 'J.B.' I didn't have the heart to tell her, so I just use it anyway. \n\nCraft fairs are getting so ridiculously expensive now, aren't they? We went to one last autumn, and this guy was selling wooden spatulas for like forty dollars. Who pays forty dollars for a spatula? I mean, I love to cook, especially making pancakes on Saturday mornings, but a cheap plastic one flips a flapjack just as well. I usually put blueberries in mine. My students always tell me I should bring some in for them, but with all the food allergies these days, you can't just bring home-baked goods into a classroom anymore. It's a shame, really. When I was a kid, people brought in cupcakes for every birthday. The ones with the thick grocery-store frosting that stained your teeth blue for the rest of the day... \n\nUm, wait. Did you ask about my phone? Or my wallet? Yeah, no, I don't really lose my stuff. I always know where it is.",
